    },
    {
      "id": "e347",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1180,
      "y": 1159,
      "width": 599.979246791946,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786153910927,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. A single row is NOT a two-row plan with one row deleted. Deleting the opposing row\ndeletes the hot aisle, and with it the entire separation strategy. Replace it\ndeliberately — chimney racks or a sealed wall plenum — or the room simply mixes.",
      "originalText": "1. A single row is NOT a two-row plan with one row deleted. Deleting the opposing row deletes the hot aisle, and with it the entire separation strategy. Replace it deliberately — chimney racks or a sealed wall plenum — or the room simply mixes.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 142,
      "versionNonce": 1522772998,
      "index": "b4a",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e348",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1180,
      "y": 1217,
      "width": 590.5797254120822,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786153910927,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. Chimney racks are the stronger answer in the narrowest rooms: they need no\nrear plenum at all, so the room can be ~2 ft shallower, and the capture is positive\nrather than relying on buoyancy.",
      "originalText": "2. Chimney racks are the stronger answer in the narrowest rooms: they need no rear plenum at all, so the room can be ~2 ft shallower, and the capture is positive rather than relying on buoyancy.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 79,
      "versionNonce": 1705082714,
      "index": "b4b",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e349",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1180,
      "y": 1273,
      "width": 598.0273136455106,
      "height": 30,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786153910927,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. If chimneys discharge into a ceiling return plenum, everything in that plenum must\nbe plenum-rated, and the suppression design must account for the plenum volume.",
      "originalText": "3. If chimneys discharge into a ceiling return plenum, everything in that plenum must be plenum-rated, and the suppression design must account for the plenum volume.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 83,
      "versionNonce": 1589394246,
      "index": "b4c",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e350",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1180,
      "y": 1311,
      "width": 613.17921423181,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786153910927,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4. Rear access is the constraint that bites. Either hold 3'-0\" behind the row, or\nspecify racks on casters with service loops in power and data so they roll forward.\nDecide before you order racks, not after.",
